  (text "GD2\nUCC27524\nSOT-23-5" (at 143 63 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "R2 10k\nsafe-default\npull-up on\nGD2 INPUT" (at 123 55 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "R3\n10R\ngate" (at 167 70 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "Q2\nIRLB3034\nN-ch D2PAK\n195A 40V" (at 191 65 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "D2\nSS310\ncatch\n100V" (at 204 68 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "SAFE DEFAULT — CRITICAL:\nR2 (10k) is on GD2 input pin, NOT on Q2 gate.\nWhen MCU is unpowered/reset, GD2 input floats HIGH via R2.\nGD2 drives Q2 gate HIGH => Q2 fully on => motor dead-shorted.\nThis is the intended safe failure mode.\nIf R2 were on Q2 gate, the gate driver would fight it." (at 15 100 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "INVERTED POLARITY — WHY:\nTIM3_CH1 is configured with inverted output polarity.\nCCR = 0         => output pin HIGH => Q2 ON  => dead short\nCCR = 2720      => PWM ~85% HIGH  => ~8ohm effective\nCCR = 3199(ARR) => output pin LOW  => Q2 OFF\nThis is the opposite of the normal PWM convention but\nguarantees the safe state at CCR=0 and at power-off." (at 15 120 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "D2 SS310 CATCH DIODE — ESSENTIAL:\nMotor inductance produces a large voltage spike on Q2 turn-off.\nUnclamped: L x dI/dt = 100uH x 20A/1us = 2000V\nQ2 Vds(max) = 40V — would be instantly destroyed.\nD2 clamps the spike at Vf + Vdc ~= 12.5V, absorbing ~20mJ.\nSS310 (100V) chosen over SS34 (40V) for headroom on 16V rail." (at 15 145 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
)
